{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793554440,"nonce":"MODYKEuzUPC+Prr5ayXuvm/qNqM=","title":"Overlay, toast and tab panel enter/exit motion from CSS keyframes","message":"dialog, sheet and drawer use MultiKeyframeAnimation presets (layout overlay.rs, overlay_stack.rs); the toast tray builds a 300 ms EaseOutCubic MultiKeyframeAnimation; tabs panels have enter/exit MultiKeyframeAnimation. Motion is defined in Rust.\n\nDo: enter and exit are @keyframes named by rules (animation on the open state, the exit animation while leaving), timed by the motion tokens; the side a sheet or drawer comes from is a custom property. The overlay layer keeps a node mounted until its exit animation ends. Related: d58924b (toast exit on web), b06a4bf (class-only keyframes on first rebuild), 8ad53a2.\n\nashui first: components/css/components.css @keyframes ui-tab-in, ui-fade-in, ui-rise-in/out, ui-toast-in/out, ui-sheet-in/out (var(--ui-sheet-from)), ui-drawer-in/out (var(--ui-drawer-from)), and how Dialog.hx / Sheet.hx / Drawer.hx / Toast.hx / Tabs.hx / Floating.hx hold a leaving node.\n\nPart of e4d2db3.","files":null}]}